          "type": "text",
          "text": "A five-year series is 140, 105, 112, 126 and 119. A report uses only years 2 to 4 and states a percentage rise. Find how many percentage points larger this reported rise is than the full-period percentage change, to the nearest whole percentage point. Enter the numerical value only."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 4,
      "primary_outcome": "1.4",
      "secondary_outcomes": [],
      "response": {
        "type": "numeric",
        "comparison_mode": "exact_numeric",
        "canonical_answer": "35",
